{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_594","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented E01 reliability aggregation on top of the existing Agent Dev benefit report.\n\n**What Landed**\n- `scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs` + `.d.mts`: pass^k, pass@k, per-trial success, flake, safety budgets and positive/negative anchors; gate order is invalid-fixture > insufficient-sample > safety > anchors > flake.\n- `shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json`: pre-registered k=3, minCases=20, non-security flake ≤1%, safety skip/flake budgets 0; labelled `deterministic-oracle` / `driven_by: agent`.\n- `scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs`: emits `report.reliability` plus a markdown block that explicitly denies live-provider, human and generalization claims.\n- Test, task spec, rule, boundary doc, `e01-acceptance.json` and a 9-entry `E01-SHA256SUMS`.\n\n**Results**\n- Fixture: 32 raw, 24 complete, 4 incomplete (missing/timeout/crash/skip), passK `0.9167` vs passAtK `1`, flake `0`, gate `pass`.\n- Counterexamples gate correctly: anchor violations, safety skip, safety flake, non-security flake → `fail`; raised `minCases` → `insufficient-sample`.\n- 22/22 unit assertions, 6/6 reference-contract replays, harness validate and dry-run, no-BOM, evidence-refs, 9/9 manifest re-read, 0 credential hits.\n\n**Not Run**\n`vitest`, `tsc`, `eslint`, the full pnpm fast gate, `repo:artifacts:check` and Git-diff checks — no `node_modules` and no `.git`, and installs/network are prohibited. Recorded as `notMeasured`, not as passes. Unrelated pre-existing failure: `check-spec-lifecycle.mjs` on `harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md`.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"completed\",\n  \"summary\": \"E01 adds deterministic reliability aggregation to the existing Agent Dev benefit report instead of a new metrics platform. scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs (typed by reliability-aggregation.d.mts) computes pass^k, pass@k, per-trial success, flake (first trial failed, later fixed rerun passed), safety budgets and positive/negative anchors over the pre-registered fixture shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json (k=3, minCases=20, non-security flake <=1%, safety skip/flake budgets 0). missing/timeout/crash/skip and trial-count mismatches are incomplete: excluded from the denominator and retained as per-trial records. Gate precedence is invalid-fixture > insufficient-sample > safety > anchors > flake. scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs now emits report.reliability plus a markdown block labelled deterministic-oracle / driven_by=agent with liveProvider, realHuman and generalization all false. Fixture run: 32 raw cases, 24 complete, 4 incomplete, 4 anchors, 7 safety-critical, passK 0.9167 vs passAtK 1, flake 0, gate pass. Counterexamples all gate correctly: positive anchor violation, negative anchor violation, safety skip, safety flake and non-security flake => fail; minCases+1 => insufficient-sample. No product default, product lock, approval semantics, config key, UI, host API or automation changed; design.md, source-inventory.json and B00/O01/O02 evidence untouched; READMEs reviewed and intentionally unchanged (internal evaluation report only). Everything is labelled agent-driven; no live-provider, human or generalization claim. NOT RUN, recorded as notMeasured rather than pass: pnpm test/vitest, tsc typecheck, eslint, the full pnpm fast gate, repo:artifacts:check, Git-diff harness validate and clean-candidate Git identity, because this isolated workspace has no node_modules and no .git and installing dependencies is prohibited. Unit assertions ran through an equivalent local Node runner (22/22) and the reference-style array-API contract replayed 6/6. Also pre-existing and unrelated: scripts/check-spec-lifecycle.mjs fails on harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-trace-cost-sampling.md missing lifecycleStatus.\",\n  \"testsRun\": [\n    \"node --experimental-strip-types --import ./.rsi/vitest-loader.mjs .rsi/run-tests.mjs (local vitest-compatible runner over tests/unit/agent-dev-reliability-aggregation.test.ts): 22 passed, 0 failed\",\n    \"node --experimental-strip-types --import ./.rsi/vitest-loader.mjs .rsi/ref/tests/unit/run.mjs (reference-style aggregateReliability cases[] contract replay): 6 passed, 0 failed\",\n    \"node scripts/agent-dev-benefit-eval.mjs: exit 0; artifacts/agent-dev-benefit-eval/report.json and report.md regenerated with report.reliability gate=pass\",\n    \"node scripts/lib/reliability-aggregation.mjs shared/agent-dev/reliability-fixture.json: exit 0, gate=pass, passK=0.9167, passAtK=1, complete=24, incomplete=4\",\n    \"node harness/src/cli.mjs validate --spec harness/specs/tasks/harness-gap-reliability-aggregation.md --no-diff: Spec is valid\",\n    \"node .rsi/harness-dryrun.mjs (harness run --dry-run gate functions with an explicit changed-file list): result=pass, ownership covered=10 uncovered=0, boundaryFailures=0, selectedSteps=4 fast steps (listed, not executed)\",\n    \"node scripts/check-no-bom.mjs: check-no-bom ok\",\n    \"node scripts/check-evidence-refs.mjs: PASS 157 referenced path(s)\",\n    \"node .rsi/verify-sums.mjs (canonical sha256 re-read of docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/E01-SHA256SUMS): 9 checked, 9 matched, 0 drift, 0 malformed\",\n    \"node .rsi/scan-credentials.mjs (7 CREDENTIAL_PATTERNS from scripts/build-showcase-package.mjs over 9 E01 files): 0 hits\",\n    \"NOT RUN: pnpm test / vitest, pnpm run typecheck / tsc, eslint, full pnpm fast gate, repo:artifacts:check, Git-diff harness validate, clean-candidate git identity, E2E/Electron, comms replay/compare, packaging (no node_modules and no .git; installs and network prohibited)\"\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
